<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wando</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wando is an island off the south-western tip of the Korean peninsula, in South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jeolla-province">Jeolla Province</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-korea">South Korea</a>. In 828 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jang-bogo">Jang Bogo</a> founded the maritime garrison of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cheonghaejin">Cheonghaejin</a> there, from which he controlled trade between Silla, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang China</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>. Today it is a county known for seaweed and abalone farming.</p></div>
